{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy gives strong forward bias in clear space, uses brief directed turns for side/front obstacles, uses backward motion only in dedicated front-recovery states, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing (uncontrollable obstacle/path events) from motion capability (controllable action events) in plant automata",
    "Use one policy specification to map sensed conditions to exactly one enabled action per decision/recovery state, plus a small progress-bias specification to prevent excessive turning/random-walk repetition"
  ],
